; A quit that reaches the renaming task while its job runs stops the job,
; which rename(2) does not wait for: the job still reports the move, so
; the buffer follows the file and files:after-rename is called. Here the
; job is stopped as it starts, as the quit's guard stops it.
> (disk-checks:write-text! "~/a.txt" "a\n")
> (define a (files:visit "~/a.txt"))
> (set! renamed '())
> (add-hook! files:after-rename note-rename)
